json5/code
description: JSON5, JSON for Humans - json/code extended with ES5 sugars
- >
  **JSON5** ("JSON for Humans") extends
  [json/code](*::language:concretes:07-json_code) with syntax sugars borrowed from
  ECMAScript 5.1 - unquoted keys, single quotes, trailing commas, comments, richer numbers. Every
  JSON code is also a valid JSON5 code:
- !!<format: text/x-json5> |
  {
    name: 'Julia',              // an unquoted key, a single-quoted string
    age: 0x2A,                  /* hexadecimal - the answer */
    pets: ['cat', 'scorpion',], // a trailing comma
  }
- >
  As in JSON, a JSON5 code is one value - structured or scalar - and comments may accompany it
  anywhere between tokens. See the subchapters below for the three parts:
- *: 00-json5_structured
- *: 01-json5_scalar
- *: 02-json5_comment
- *..:07-json_code
